{"text": " You wake up in 1537 in a French army camp near Turin, smoke, drums, and the groans of wounded men. Did you know that the usual treatment for a gunshot wound here is boiling oil? The surgeons believe gunpowder poisons the flesh. Here's your patient, a soldier with a gunshot wound. Doctors here teach that illness comes from four fluids in the body and that the cure is to balance them so they burn the wound, or they purge, or they drain some blood. One young army surgeon, Ambrose Paray, runs out of oil. So he mixes egg yolk, rose oil, and turpentine instead. By his own account, the men he treated that way slept better with less swelling. He wrote it down years later. Historians still argue about how much of the story is legend. How long do you live? In England, a newborn could expect about 35 years, mostly because so many children died. So what is medicine to you? Balance, the body is a scale in the doctor adjusted. Bleeding stays in fashion for centuries. And in 1799, it finds its most famous patient.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 3.42, "text": " You wake up in 1537 in a French army camp near Turin,", "tokens": [50364, 509, 6634, 493, 294, 2119, 12851, 294, 257, 5522, 7267, 2255, 2651, 5712, 259, 11, 50566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1355786853366428, "compression_ratio": 1.6151079136690647, "no_speech_prob": 0.016472311690449715, "words": [{"word": " You", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.14, "probability": 0.7923716902732849}, {"word": " wake", "start": 0.14, "end": 0.28, "probability": 0.9919909834861755}, {"word": " up", "start": 0.28, "end": 0.46, "probability": 0.9994949102401733}, {"word": " in", "start": 0.46, "end": 0.58, "probability": 0.9916191101074219}, {"word": " 1537", "start": 0.58, "end": 1.54, "probability": 0.9910514652729034}, {"word": " in", "start": 1.54, "end": 1.78, "probability": 0.8231023550033569}, {"word": " a", "start": 1.78, "end": 1.86, "probability": 0.9976264834403992}, {"word": " French", "start